course: dictionary
lesson: 15494
title: One word, three meanings: studied
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Studied is the past form of study. To study something is to learn about it by reading, practising or thinking hard. «Mia studied fractions all week.» That means she learned about fractions over the whole week.
explain: Studied can also mean looked at something carefully for a long time. «The scientists studied the frogs in the pond.» They watched the frogs closely to find out how they live. Look at the words around studied to see which meaning fits.
explain: As a rare adjective, studied means done on purpose and carefully planned, not natural. «His studied answer sounded as if he had practised it for days.» Nothing about it felt spontaneous. To check, swap in learned, looked at carefully or planned, and see which one makes the sentence make sense.
fact: Studied is the past form of study: study, studies, studied, studying.
fact: «Studied» can mean learned about something by reading, practising or thinking about it.
fact: «Studied» can mean looked at something carefully for a long time.
fact: As an adjective, «studied» is rare and means done on purpose and carefully planned.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «We studied fractions all week.» What does studied mean here? | Painted | Ate quickly | *Learned about | Lost track of
exercise: «The scientists studied the frogs in the pond for an hour.» What does studied mean here? | *Looked at carefully for a long time | Forgot | Ran away from | Spoke loudly about
exercise: «Her studied answer sounded as if she had practised it for days.» What does studied mean here? | *Done on purpose and carefully planned, not natural | Quickly thrown away | Learned at school | Sung loudly
test: «Sam studied the map to find the way home.» What does studied mean here? | Learned | *Looked at carefully | Folded up | Stayed away from
test: «Ella studied for her spelling test every night.» Which word is the past form of study? | *Studied | Study | Studying | Studies
exam: «Tom studied his friend's face and saw that he was worried.» What does studied mean here? | *Looked at carefully for a long time | Ignored | Painted | Read aloud
